Receiver: a phone invited right after pairing is remembered before an idle release ends its session (2026-10-19).

On the F50, a newly paired iPhone was invited at once with no page open for more than the idle wait: its
session came up and the very next supervisor pass released it, before the pass that would learn the phone's
Wi-Fi identity ("remember"). Opening the page later found no known phone on the Wi-Fi, so no invitation went
out and the page stayed on "waiting for the iPhone" until the settings page invited that phone by hand. The
identity is now learned first in each pass, before the idle decision.

